    {
      "path": "src/micropython/lib",
      "control": "not-ours",
      "provenance": "vendored-upstream",
      "note": "MicroPython's repository layout designates lib/ as third-party code, which is the basis for this rule and covers the directories vendored in-tree rather than as submodules (libm, littlefs, oofatfs, re1.5, uzlib and the rest). Submodules beneath it match their own longer-prefix rules above, so a newly added one still fails loudly. Unverified where it matters most: a fork delta under lib/ would be classified vendored by this rule, and the delta is not computable while the src/micropython submodule has no upstream remote configured."
    },
